              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਨੀਲਾ — nīlā — blue, masculine singular direct ਨੀਲੀ (nili) — nīlī — blue, feminine singular direct."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For this one form, change the final -ਾ ending of familiar ਨੀਲਾ to feminine singular -ੀ. The result is ਨੀਲੀ (nili). Keep the stem and meaning steady; only the ending changes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: source boundary",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Punjabi University Patiala's reference grammar says that inflectable adjectives agree with their head noun in gender, number, and case. Its noun-phrase examples contrast masculine ਚੰਗਾ ਮੁੰਡਾ with feminine ਚੰਗੀ ਕੁੜੀ. Source: Punjabi University reference grammar."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That source supports this one feminine singular direct ending change. This chapter does not teach a full agreement paradigm, plural or oblique forms, a new colour, or a general contrast between attributive and predicative uses."
            }
          ]
        },
